# Gloss configuration.
#
# Copy this file to ".env" (same folder) and fill in the provider you use.
# install.command will do it for you if you'd rather be walked through it.
#
# .env is gitignored — your key never lands in the repository.
#
# Gloss talks to any endpoint that speaks the OpenAI chat-completions API,
# so "OpenAI-compatible" covers far more than OpenAI.

# Which provider to use: openai | anthropic | tamu | openrouter | ollama | custom
GLOSS_PROVIDER=tamu

# Optional. Overrides the provider's default model. Required for the providers
# marked below, because there is no default that is safe to assume.
#GLOSS_MODEL=

# Optional. Only for GLOSS_PROVIDER=custom.
#GLOSS_BASE_URL=

# Optional. Parallel requests. Defaults to 8 for hosted providers, 2 for local
# ones — a single local model server queues rather than parallelizes.
#GLOSS_WORKERS=


# --- OpenAI --------------------------------------------------------------
# https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
#OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# --- Anthropic -----------------------------------------------------------
# https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
# Uses Anthropic's OpenAI-compatible layer, which they document as intended for
# testing and comparison rather than as a production surface. Model ids look
# like claude-sonnet-5 or claude-haiku-4-5.
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# --- TAMU AI (free with a Texas A&M NetID) --------------------------------
# chat.tamu.ai -> Settings -> API Key
# Also read from ~/.config/tamu-ai/api-key if you already have that set up.
#TAMU_AI_API_KEY=sk-...

# --- OpenRouter (one key, most vendors) -----------------------------------
# https://openrouter.ai/keys — reaches Anthropic, Google, Meta and others.
# GLOSS_MODEL is REQUIRED; ids are "vendor/model", e.g. anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5
#OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...

# --- Ollama (a model running on this Mac) ---------------------------------
# No key, no cost, and the document never leaves the machine.
# Start it with:  ollama serve      (and `ollama pull <model>` to add models)
# GLOSS_MODEL is REQUIRED — set it to a model you have pulled, e.g. qwen3.6
# Expect this to be SLOW. Measured with qwen3.6 (23GB) on an Apple Silicon Mac:
# ~70s for the whole-document pass and ~84s per paragraph, so roughly an hour
# for a 76-paragraph paper (TAMU does the same paper in about a minute).
# A paper is ~115,000 input tokens and local prompt processing is far slower.
# For usable speed locally, pull a small model:  ollama pull qwen3:4b

# --- Anything else ---------------------------------------------------------
# GLOSS_PROVIDER=custom reaches any other OpenAI-compatible endpoint —
# Google Gemini, Groq, Together, Fireworks, DeepSeek, LM Studio, vLLM.
# Set GLOSS_BASE_URL and GLOSS_MODEL, and put the key in GLOSS_API_KEY.
#GLOSS_API_KEY=
